/* book: lead: The air in a cylinder is never still. The inlet port, the valve and the piston set up organised, large-scale motions: swirl, a rotation about the cylinder axis; tumble, a rotation about an axis across the cylinder; and squish, a radial inward flow as the piston nears the head at TDC. Near TDC these motions break down into turbulence. In a CI engine they mix the injected fuel with air; in an SI eng */
