/* book exam traps: Squish is a radial inward flow near TDC, not a rotation; swirl and tumble are rotations. | Swirl rotates about the cylinder axis; tumble rotates about an axis across the cylinder. Do not swap the axes. | The swirl ratio has no unit: both speeds are in rev/min (or both in rad/s). | Organised motion is not turbulence; it decays into turbulence near TDC. | More swirl is not always better: it raises heat loss, can overlap the spray plumes and cuts volumetric efficiency. */
