/* book exam traps: The hemispherical chamber has the lowest surface-to-volume ratio of the common SI shapes, so low heat loss; its weak point is little squish, not a large surface. | A pre-chamber or swirl-chamber engine is indirect injection; direct injection sprays into a bowl in the piston. | The bowl is part of the clearance volume; do not add it again when finding the compression ratio. | IDI runs quieter and tolerates poor fuel, but DI gives the better fuel economy and cold starting. | Convert bowl depth from mm to cm before working in cm³. */
